Store procedure calls
Method 1: Using Spring Data JPA (@Procedure)This is the cleanest and most common approach for standard procedures.1. Define the Stored Procedure in your EntityUse @NamedStoredProcedureQueries if your procedure returns data or has complex parameters.java@Entity
@Table(name = "EMPLOYEES")
@NamedStoredProcedureQuery(
    name = "Employee.get_salary_grade",
    procedureName = "GET_SALARY_GRADE",
    parameters = {
        @StoredProcedureParameter(mode = ParameterMode.IN, name = "emp_id", type = Long.class),
        @StoredProcedureParameter(mode = ParameterMode.OUT, name = "salary_grade", type = String.class)
    }
)
public class Employee {
    @Id
    private Long id;
    // other fields, getters, setters
}
Use code with caution.2. Call it in your RepositoryReference the named query or map the procedure directly using the @Procedure annotation.java@Repository
public interface EmployeeRepository extends JpaRepository<Employee, Long> {
    
    // Approach A: Using the Named Stored Procedure
    @Procedure(name = "Employee.get_salary_grade")
    String getSalaryGradeNamed(@Param("emp_id") Long empId);

    // Approach B: Directly mapping by method name (must match procedure name in DB)
    @Procedure(procedureName = "GET_SALARY_GRADE")
    String getSalaryGradeDirect(@Param("emp_id") Long empId);
}
Method 2: Using EntityManager (Dynamic Calls)If you do not want to declare annotations on your entities, or if your parameters are dynamic, use the EntityManager.java@Service
public class EmployeeService {

    @Autowired
    private EntityManager entityManager;

    public String getSalaryGrade(Long empId) {
        StoredProcedureQuery query = entityManager.createStoredProcedureQuery("GET_SALARY_GRADE");
        
        // Register parameters
        query.registerStoredProcedureParameter("emp_id", Long.class, ParameterMode.IN);
        query.registerStoredProcedureParameter("salary_grade", String.class, ParameterMode.OUT);
        
        // Set values and execute
        query.setParameter("emp_id", empId);
        query.execute();
        
        // Get output
        return (String) query.getOutputParameterValue("salary_grade");
    }
